menu "MTK3 ESP-MESH"

config ESPMESH_CHANNEL
    int "Mesh WiFi channel"
    default 6
    range 1 13
    help
        All nodes in the mesh must use the same channel.  1/6/11 overlap
        least with BLE advertising channels if BLE coexists later.

config ESPMESH_MAX_LAYER
    int "Max mesh layer (tree depth)"
    default 2
    range 1 25

config ESPMESH_AP_PASSWORD
    string "Mesh inter-node AP password"
    default "mtk3mesh1"

config ESPMESH_ROUTER_SSID
    string "Upstream router SSID"
    default "YOUR_ROUTER_SSID"
    help
        Set this to your own WiFi network before building the ESP-MESH
        examples.  The root node associates to this router; a non-root node
        must carry the same router config even when it reaches the network
        only through its mesh parent.

        Note ESPMESH_CHANNEL must match this router's actual WiFi channel -
        the mesh child does not scan or switch channels.

config ESPMESH_ROUTER_PASSWORD
    string "Upstream router password"
    default ""
    help
        Your router's WPA2 password.  Left empty by default so the value is
        never carried in the repository; set it with
        `idf.py -C examples/ble_espmesh_root menuconfig` under "MTK3 ESP-MESH",
        or edit the example's sdkconfig.defaults locally.

endmenu
